# Normalise line endings to LF in the repository.
#
# This is not cosmetic. Git's autocrlf on Windows rewrites text files to CRLF in
# the working tree, and several files in this repository are consumed by Linux
# processes that care:
#
#   Dockerfile          a CRLF continuation backslash breaks the build
#   *.sh                "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M"
#   *.yml, *.yaml       Ansible and compose parse CRLF fine, but diffs churn
#   *.j2, *.tftpl       systemd unit files tolerate CRLF, but the rendered
#                       directive values can carry a trailing \r into a path
#
# Forcing LF here means the checked-out file is correct regardless of the local
# core.autocrlf setting, which is the only way a repository can be reliably
# reproducible across Windows and Linux contributors.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit, because these are the ones where a stray \r is a real failure.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.j2 text eol=lf
*.tftpl text eol=lf
*.tf text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf

# Python and docs: LF, matching the formatter.
*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.cfg text eol=lf
*.ini text eol=lf

# Binary: never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz binary
*.npz binary
*.pt binary
*.onnx binary
*.ts binary
*.docx binary
*.pdf binary
